## Why This Is Asked

This question assesses a candidate's ability to translate product goals into a financially grounded technical plan, balancing on-device ML costs, user privacy, and rollout risk.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML cost modeling (energy, memory, inference latency)
- Data transfer savings and network impact
- Privacy controls and regulatory compliance
- OTA update cadence and maintenance costs
- Rollout strategy, drift monitoring, and go/no-go criteria

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-cost model for CBA calculations
function cba(params) {
  const energy = params.inferences * params.energyPerInference;
  const memory = params.modelSize + params.cacheSize;
  const dataSavings = params.uploadSize * params.reductionRate;
  return { energy, memory, dataSavings };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assess understanding of privacy-preserving, on-device analytics and the viability of data-sharing via aggregates.

## Key Concepts

- On-device analytics and data minimization
- User consent and opt-in UX
- Aggregated data leakage risk and privacy controls
- Cost modeling: device runtime, memory, and backend bandwidth
- Rollout strategy, drift monitoring, and governance

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple rolling aggregate for 90-day window on-device
function rollingAvg(values, window=90) {
  let sum=0;
  const res=[];
  for(let i=0;i<values.length;i++){
    sum+=values[i];
    if(i>=window) sum-=values[i-window];
    if(i>=window-1) res.push(sum/(window));
  }
  return res;
}
```

